Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?dos:=20Phase=2011=20patch=200050=20=E2=80=94=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?DOS=20GetDeviceBuf=20quiescence=20gate=20(Phase=2012=20Option?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20A)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Iter K IDLEPROB v2 confirmed slot 0048 mechanism works (DSP 0xD5 halts
IRQ-5 cleanly on operator's SB16-PnP CTL0026 + DSP v4.13) but in-
gameplay yield = 0.26 ms / flip because the DAC ring is continuously
filled and never drains long enough for auto-engage to fire.

Root cause: SDL3's PlaybackAudioThread runs Iterate→WaitDevice
continuously. DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf returns the staging buffer
unconditionally; SDL_audio.c:1230 falls into SDL_memset silence-fill
when no streams have data; PlayDevice writes silence to the SB16 ring;
ring stays full; ISR drains chunk by chunk; auto-engage silent-IRQ
counter never crosses threshold; DSP never pauses.

Fix: GetDeviceBuf walks device->logical_devices->bound_streams calling
SDL_GetAudioStreamAvailable on each. If all return 0 → set
*buffer_size = 0 + SDL_Delay(10). Audio thread's SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate
at SDL_audio.c:1189 enters the "abandon iteration" branch, skips
PlayDevice. Ring drains via IRQ; 4 silent IRQs trip auto-engage; DSP
pause issued; IRQ-5 stops; fps recovered.

The SDL_Delay(10) throttle is critical: when main thread is blocked
elsewhere (engine logic loops, user-side SDL_Delay), DOS_Yield is a
no-op (no other runnable thread); without an active sleep, audio
thread spins burning CPU. SDL_Delay(10) advances wall-clock via
uclock()-polling so other time-blocked threads can wake. ~100 iter/sec
audio thread loop is well below buffer rate (43 Hz @ 22050/512), so
SFX-trigger latency unaffected.

Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE=0 disables the
gate (returns staging_buffer unconditionally; pre-0050 always-fill-ring
behavior; auto-engage idle-pause cannot fire). Default ON. Strict-"0"
match per CLAUDE.md env-var convention. Cached at module scope; resolved
once at OpenDevice time to avoid SDL_GetHint per-call cost in hot path.

Killswitch motivation per team-lead's iter L dispatch: PLAY1 (treatment,
gate active default) − PLAY2 (control, gate killswitched) = within-iter
SDL/0050 isolation signal. Without env-var killswitch, both PLAYs would
have identical audio config; cross-iter comparison vs iter K would
absorb any drift. The env var enables clean within-iter measurement.

Mirrors SDL3's existing SDL_AudioGetDeviceBuf_Default WASAPI pattern at
SDL_audio.c:867 (buffer_size=0 = "skip iteration"). Pattern is
well-tested upstream; this patch extends it to the DOS backend.

Resume: when engine fires SFX trigger → mixer queues data into a stream
→ next GetDeviceBuf finds available > 0 → returns staging_buffer
normally → PlayDevice's auto-resume gate (line ~828) detects DSP paused
+ !g_dos_audio_force_dsp_pause → 0xD6 sent → DSP resumes → IRQ-5
resumes → SFX plays. Latency: <1 audio thread iter cycle.

Hot-path cost: walking bound_streams ≈ sub-µs per check on Cave Story
(1-2 typical bound streams). The SDL_Delay(10) only fires on the
quiescent path (no streams have data); during normal mixing the gate
returns staging_buffer immediately.

Edge case — Tier-1 Organya path uses MIX_HookMusic (callback). Mixer
queues hook output to a stream so the gate sees available > 0 and falls
through to default path. Phase-10 OPL3 default null-hooks MIX_HookMusic
so SB16 sees no callback path; gate engages cleanly during silent
gameplay.

Predicted savings (per `perf_predictions_unreliable.md`): -8 to -12 ms
per flip during silent gameplay (full IRQ-5 elimination). 0 during
active SFX. Real-HW iter L IDLEPROB v3 + actual gameplay PLAY logs are
the validation gate.

Validation status:
- Gameplay smoke (DOSBox-X with --fast): GREEN. Game launches, hits
  title, accepts input, no crash, 8 screenshots clean.
- SDLPROBE smoke under DOSBox-X: structurally limited per
  `dosbox_not_behavioral_proxy_for_io.md`. Probe's
  scenario_audio_callback_entry opens a stream with no data while main
  thread is in SDL_Delay(3000); cooperative-scheduler edge case under
  emulation differs from real-HW behavior. Real-HW iter L is the data
  gate. PLAY2 control with killswitch=0 reverts to pre-0050 behavior
  for clean drift comparison.

One TU touched (vendor/SDL/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c). ~95 lines
added across the OpenDevice killswitch resolve + GetDeviceBuf gate logic.
No new public API. New env var SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE
documented in docs/BOOT.md (user-facing/fallback section).

Cross-reference: docs/PHASE12-PIXTONE-DECOUPLE-DESIGN.md Option A.
Companion patches: SDL/0037 (idle-pause API + auto-engage IRQ-counter),
SDL/0038 (SB16 IRQ-5 instrumentation), SDL/0048 (ForcePause auto-resume
race fix). Slot 0050 is the missing piece that lets the existing
auto-engage detector actually fire under SDL3-DOS architecture.
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 90 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 89 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index b6cd35b3d..e41b4d79a 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -55,6 +55,16 @@ static int soundblaster_version_minor = -1;
 static bool soundblaster_is_sb16 = false; // false when FORCE_SB_8BIT or DSP < 4
 static Uint8 soundblaster_silence_value = 0;
 
+/* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0050): killswitch state for the
+   GetDeviceBuf quiescence gate. Default ON (false = gate engages); set
+   SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE=0 to flip to true and
+   disable (revert to pre-0050 always-return-staging behavior). Per
+   CLAUDE.md strict-"0" env-var convention: only literal "0" disables;
+   any other value leaves gate active. Resolved once at OpenDevice time;
+   read by DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf in the hot path. Used by iter L
+   PLAY2 control measurement to isolate SDL/0050 effect within iter. */
+static bool g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled = false;
+
 static void ResetSoundBlasterDSP(void)
 {
     // reset the DSP.
@@ -485,6 +495,25 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
 {
     const bool is_sb16 = soundblaster_is_sb16;
 
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0050): resolve quiescence-gate
+       killswitch once at OpenDevice time. Strict-"0" match per CLAUDE.md
+       env-var convention. Cached at module scope; read by
+       DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf in the hot path. */
+    {
+        const char *gate_hint = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE");
+        g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled =
+            (gate_hint && gate_hint[0] == '0' && gate_hint[1] == 0);
+        if (g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled) {
+            doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE=0 "
+                             "(SDL/0050 quiescence gate DISABLED; pre-0050 always-"
+                             "fill-ring behavior; auto-engage idle-pause cannot fire)");
+        } else {
+            doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0050 quiescence gate active (default); "
+                             "GetDeviceBuf returns *buffer_size=0 when no streams "
+                             "have data → auto-engage path can fire on silent gameplay");
+        }
+    }
+
     if (is_sb16) {
         // SB16 (DSP >= 4): 16-bit stereo signed
         device->spec.format = SDL_AUDIO_S16LE;
@@ -795,7 +824,66 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
 static Uint8 *DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf(SDL_AudioDevice *device, int *buffer_size)
 {
     struct SDL_PrivateAudioData *hidden = device->hidden;
-    (void)buffer_size; // unchanged, always one chunk
+
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0050, Phase 12 Option A): GetDeviceBuf
+       quiescence gate. Returns *buffer_size = 0 to signal "skip this audio-
+       thread iteration" when no logical-device bound streams have data.
+       Mirrors SDL3's SDL_AudioGetDeviceBuf_Default WASAPI pattern at
+       SDL_audio.c:867, where buffer_size=0 makes SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate
+       at SDL_audio.c:1189 enter the "abandon iteration" branch and skip the
+       PlayDevice call entirely.
+
+       Mechanism + motivation per docs/PHASE12-PIXTONE-DECOUPLE-DESIGN.md:
+       SDL3's audio thread runs Iterate→WaitDevice continuously, filling the
+       SB16 ring with silence (SDL_audio.c:1230 SDL_memset fallback) when no
+       streams have data. Ring stays full; ISR keeps draining; auto-engage
+       silent-IRQ counter never crosses threshold; idle-pause never fires.
+
+       Iter K IDLEPROB v2 confirmed slot 0048 mechanism works (DSP 0xD5 halts
+       IRQ-5 cleanly) but in-gameplay yield = 0.26 ms because the ring stayed
+       continuously filled. This patch is the missing piece: when audio
+       quiescent, GetDeviceBuf returns buffer_size=0 → audio thread skips
+       PlayDevice → ring drains via IRQ → 4 silent IRQs trip auto-engage →
+       DSP pause → IRQ-5 stops → fps recovered.
+
+       Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE=0 disables
+       the gate (returns staging_buffer unconditionally; pre-0050 behavior).
+       Iter L PLAY2 (control) sets this env var; PLAY1 (treatment) leaves
+       unset. Within-iter PLAY1−PLAY2 = SDL/0050 isolation signal.
+
+       The SDL_Delay(10) inside the gate path throttles audio thread to
+       ~100 iter/sec when quiescent, preventing CPU spin under cooperative
+       scheduler when main thread is also time-blocked. */
+    if (!g_dos_audio_quiescence_gate_disabled && device->logical_devices != NULL) {
+        bool any_data = false;
+        SDL_LogicalAudioDevice *logdev = device->logical_devices;
+        while (logdev != NULL && !any_data) {
+            SDL_AudioStream *stream = logdev->bound_streams;
+            while (stream != NULL) {
+                if (SDL_GetAudioStreamAvailable(stream) > 0) {
+                    any_data = true;
+                    break;
+                }
+                stream = stream->next_binding;
+            }
+            logdev = logdev->next;
+        }
+        if (!any_data) {
+            *buffer_size = 0;  /* skip this iteration; audio thread does
+                                  GetDeviceBuf → buffer_size==0 → return
+                                  without calling PlayDevice */
+            SDL_Delay(10);      /* throttle audio thread to ~100 iter/sec
+                                   when quiescent. Prevents CPU spin when
+                                   main thread is blocked on SDL_Delay
+                                   (DOS_Yield is a no-op then; only SDL_Delay
+                                   advances time-keyed wake mechanisms). */
+            return hidden->staging_buffer;
+        }
+    }
+
+    /* Default path: at least one bound stream has data (or gate disabled
+       via killswitch); return staging buffer for normal mix → PlayDevice
+       → ring write → IRQ drain. */
     return hidden->staging_buffer;
 }
 
